1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:02,625
[laughing] Yes!

2
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:04,791
Looks like a geyser
just gone off!

3
00:00:04,791 --> 00:00:06,250
Fresh salvage!

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:08,250
Wait till you see
all this, Cole!

5
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,208
So there's junk everywhere
in the Land of Lost Things,

6
00:00:11,208 --> 00:00:13,708
but you're excited
about this particular junk?

7
00:00:13,708 --> 00:00:15,208
We're in Sector Four!

8
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:18,083
Lots of quality gear
spews out in Sector Four.

9
00:00:18,083 --> 00:00:20,041
You've got a lot
to learn, newbie.

10
00:00:20,041 --> 00:00:21,083
[laughing]

11
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:24,833
[gasping] A new book!

12
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:27,208
"Boobytraps
and How to Survive Them."

13
00:00:27,208 --> 00:00:30,458
Huh, people sure seem to lose
a lot of copies of these.

14
00:00:30,458 --> 00:00:32,375
[Spitz] Cool!
Look what I found!

15
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:33,708
[roaring]

16
00:00:33,708 --> 00:00:36,250
[screaming]

17
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,583
[cawing]

18
00:00:37,583 --> 00:00:38,500
[yelping] No! No, no, no, no!

19
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,416
It's back, it's back!

20
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:41,875
[gasping and sobbing]

21
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:42,875
Fritz!

22
00:00:42,875 --> 00:00:44,583
I'm sorry, I forgot!

23
00:00:44,583 --> 00:00:47,083
Fritz's village
was attacked by a monster.

24
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:49,625
It's how he ended up here.

25
00:00:49,625 --> 00:00:50,541
Fritz, it's okay.

26
00:00:50,541 --> 00:00:51,750
Spitz didn't mean it.

27
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:53,083
You're safe.

28
00:00:53,083 --> 00:00:55,375
[sighing] I am?

29
00:00:55,375 --> 00:00:56,333
Sure.

30
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:57,833
You'll always be safe with me.

31
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:59,250
All of you.

32
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:01,000
<i>[Kai's voice] ...Cole?</i>

33
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,625
Cole...?

34
00:01:02,625 --> 00:01:04,541
Cole! Are you still with us?

35
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:06,875
[Cole] The trail's leading
straight to Imperium.

36
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:08,208
Come on!

37
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:18,750
[people panicking]

38
00:01:25,291 --> 00:01:26,458
[screaming]

39
00:01:28,375 --> 00:01:29,250
[gasping]

40
00:01:39,458 --> 00:01:40,708
Where's Nokt?

41
00:01:40,708 --> 00:01:41,833
He's the one behind this,

42
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:44,791
and we gotta get the Finders
back to normal.

43
00:01:44,791 --> 00:01:46,208
I don't see him anywhere!

44
00:01:46,208 --> 00:01:47,833
[Percival] Everyone!
Get to cover!

45
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:50,166
There's too many of them! Run!

46
00:01:58,791 --> 00:02:00,291
[snarling]

47
00:02:00,291 --> 00:02:03,583
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

48
00:02:03,583 --> 00:02:06,500
♪ Together we will rise ♪

49
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:09,958
♪ We fight ♪

50
00:02:09,958 --> 00:02:13,083
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

51
00:02:15,291 --> 00:02:16,625
No!

52
00:02:16,625 --> 00:02:18,958
Roby, talk to me!

53
00:02:18,958 --> 00:02:19,833
[roaring affectionately]

54
00:02:19,833 --> 00:02:22,083
Womp womp...

55
00:02:22,083 --> 00:02:24,750
Just like all the people
in the Land of Lee.

56
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:26,625
Yeah, but with this guy,
being hollow

57
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:29,041
really improves
his personality, am I right?

58
00:02:29,041 --> 00:02:30,000
Ah!

59
00:02:30,875 --> 00:02:33,083
Don't insult my boyfriend!

60
00:02:33,083 --> 00:02:34,083
Hold up,

61
00:02:34,083 --> 00:02:37,083
you actually, unironically
like that guy?

62
00:02:37,083 --> 00:02:38,041
For real?

63
00:02:38,041 --> 00:02:40,000
With all his "stangs"
and his "zoots"

64
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,416
and his "womp, womp."

65
00:02:41,416 --> 00:02:42,875
He's like if the sound
of an airhorn

66
00:02:42,875 --> 00:02:44,416
became a person.

67
00:02:44,416 --> 00:02:47,208
That beautiful genius
is worth more than ten of you,

68
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:49,625
you goodness-shattered freak
with bad breath!

69
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:51,666
[sniffing]

70
00:02:53,083 --> 00:02:54,250
Stop this!

71
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:55,375
Roby being hollow

72
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:57,500
also means we can't learn
how to stop ThunderFang

73
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,083
and his Spectral Invasions.

74
00:03:00,541 --> 00:03:02,916
[Arin] Maybe they could help?

75
00:03:02,916 --> 00:03:05,166
The Security Bots! Of course!

76
00:03:05,166 --> 00:03:06,500
No souls to drain.

77
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,541
Excuse us,

78
00:03:07,541 --> 00:03:08,750
we need information

79
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:10,083
on the ancient battle between--

80
00:03:10,083 --> 00:03:11,541
The lore
of the City of Temples

81
00:03:11,541 --> 00:03:13,250
cannot be granted to the public

82
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:14,791
without an appropriate order.

83
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:15,833
Okay.

84
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:17,708
I order you to tell us about--

85
00:03:17,708 --> 00:03:18,958
[bot] Order rejected.

86
00:03:18,958 --> 00:03:20,458
Unauthorized user.

87
00:03:20,458 --> 00:03:22,041
Please apply
to Gamesmaster Roby

88
00:03:22,041 --> 00:03:23,166
for authorization.

89
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:25,250
Womp, womp...

90
00:03:25,250 --> 00:03:27,625
That's not happening
any time soon.

91
00:03:27,625 --> 00:03:29,166
So this is just a dead end?

92
00:03:29,166 --> 00:03:30,416
There's still one person

93
00:03:30,416 --> 00:03:32,291
who can tell us
what we need to know,

94
00:03:32,291 --> 00:03:34,500
if he hasn't been
hollowed out too.

95
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:35,375
Who?

96
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:36,833
You won't like it.

97
00:03:36,833 --> 00:03:38,333
Come on.

98
00:03:38,333 --> 00:03:40,208
We're going to the dungeons.

99
00:03:41,166 --> 00:03:42,541
[unearthly shrieking]

100
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,333
The Red Ninja?

101
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:48,625
Thank the Sources!

102
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:50,875
H'ah!

103
00:03:50,875 --> 00:03:52,625
I'm gonna mess you goons up.

104
00:03:52,625 --> 00:03:53,625
Hey'ah!

105
00:03:53,625 --> 00:03:57,250
And you brought... some guy.

106
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:58,458
H'yah! Ha!

107
00:03:58,458 --> 00:03:59,625
A little to the left!

108
00:03:59,625 --> 00:04:01,000
No, uh, your left.

109
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,625
Okay, more... more...

110
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:03,625
Almost.

111
00:04:03,625 --> 00:04:05,208
[unearthly shrieking]

112
00:04:05,208 --> 00:04:06,208
H'yah!

113
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:07,458
[Frak] I definitely
hit some too.

114
00:04:07,458 --> 00:04:08,416
[Cole] I'm sure.

115
00:04:10,958 --> 00:04:12,833
Prismatic Steel.

116
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:14,541
Like the lenses in my goggles.

117
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:15,708
[unearthly shrieking]

118
00:04:15,708 --> 00:04:17,083
Can we use those?

119
00:04:17,083 --> 00:04:18,833
I'm kinda in the middle
of using this, Percival.

120
00:04:18,833 --> 00:04:19,791
No, we need--

121
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:21,791
[instrument blowing
spectral note]

122
00:04:24,041 --> 00:04:26,833
[blowing spectral note]

123
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:28,375
The souls of the people
they're draining

124
00:04:28,375 --> 00:04:29,666
are going in that thing!

125
00:04:29,666 --> 00:04:32,041
That must be the key
to saving the Finders!

126
00:04:32,041 --> 00:04:33,708
[blowing spectral note]

127
00:04:36,916 --> 00:04:38,166
[groaning] Ugh...

128
00:04:38,166 --> 00:04:41,083
This walking tour
gets negative five stars.

129
00:04:41,083 --> 00:04:43,125
Do not recommend.

130
00:04:43,125 --> 00:04:45,333
Could you just tell us
why we're here, Wyldfyre?

131
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:47,416
To talk to the traitor.

132
00:04:47,416 --> 00:04:49,166
Roby's Uncle Bleckt?

133
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:52,291
The old jerk was
Mr. Ledger-meister or whatever.

134
00:04:52,291 --> 00:04:55,541
If anyone knows what we need
to know, it's him.

135
00:04:55,541 --> 00:04:57,500
Oh, wait, so the plan

136
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,875
is trust the guy
who made a deal with Ras

137
00:04:59,875 --> 00:05:01,875
to backstab his own nephew?

138
00:05:01,875 --> 00:05:03,833
[laughing derisively]
This'll go great.

139
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:05,041
Halt.

140
00:05:05,041 --> 00:05:07,791
The prisoner is not allowed
unauthorized visitors.

141
00:05:07,791 --> 00:05:09,333
This is an emergency.

142
00:05:09,333 --> 00:05:11,833
The fate of the Merged Lands
hangs in the balance.

143
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:14,791
Access denied
by order of the Gamesmaster.

144
00:05:14,791 --> 00:05:16,958
Guess they only listen to Roby.

145
00:05:18,666 --> 00:05:20,625
You heard the lady.
Back away!

146
00:05:20,625 --> 00:05:22,250
Negative.

147
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:23,750
Unauthorized user.

148
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:24,750
Fine.

149
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:27,125
Then eat lightning!

150
00:05:28,375 --> 00:05:29,958
Negative. We are not hungry.

151
00:05:29,958 --> 00:05:32,375
These bots were designed
as security

152
00:05:32,375 --> 00:05:33,583
for the Tournament
of the Sources.

153
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:35,583
Elemental powers
aren't gonna work on them.

154
00:05:35,583 --> 00:05:37,208
Let's see if feet work.

155
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:38,041
No, wait!

156
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,541
Alert!

157
00:05:40,541 --> 00:05:41,916
We are under attack!

158
00:05:41,916 --> 00:05:43,375
Defend and apprehend!

159
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:46,166
H'yah!

160
00:05:47,291 --> 00:05:48,666
[grunting with effort]

161
00:05:59,708 --> 00:06:00,875
Ha! H'yup!

162
00:06:00,875 --> 00:06:02,000
Hey!

163
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,375
Back off!

164
00:06:08,708 --> 00:06:10,458
Hey, bots...

165
00:06:10,458 --> 00:06:12,041
Do jumping jacks.

166
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,625
Now dance a jig.

167
00:06:17,625 --> 00:06:19,041
[♪♪♪]

168
00:06:20,583 --> 00:06:22,208
What's the deal here?

169
00:06:22,208 --> 00:06:24,000
Gamesmaster Roby instructed us

170
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,291
that should he ever
become incapacitated

171
00:06:26,291 --> 00:06:28,916
that User Wyldfyre
is to be afforded

172
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:30,375
all-access authority.

173
00:06:30,375 --> 00:06:32,541
I'm his backup contact?

174
00:06:32,541 --> 00:06:34,333
Oh, Roby, you cutie!

175
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:39,333
Hmm, so I basically
command my own city now?

176
00:06:39,333 --> 00:06:41,500
Interesting.

177
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,833
Interesting...

178
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,750
Romantic relationships
make no sense to me.

179
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:50,500
Especially
this romantic relationship.

180
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,666
Wyldfyre, we're still
on a mission.

181
00:06:52,666 --> 00:06:53,916
Get the bots
to take us to Bleckt.

182
00:06:53,916 --> 00:06:55,750
Of course.

183
00:06:59,291 --> 00:07:01,375
These are seedless, right?

184
00:07:01,375 --> 00:07:03,833
Roby would want me
to have seedless.

185
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:10,166
I knew it'd go to her head,
just not this fast.

186
00:07:10,166 --> 00:07:13,791
To what do I owe this...
"honor," hmm?

187
00:07:13,791 --> 00:07:16,833
Come to gloat
about my fall from grace?

188
00:07:16,833 --> 00:07:19,000
We're here about the invasion.

189
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,500
Invasion?

190
00:07:20,500 --> 00:07:21,625
You don't know?

191
00:07:21,625 --> 00:07:23,875
The isolation of this cell

192
00:07:23,875 --> 00:07:25,583
has put a knowledge of history

193
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:28,083
even more firmly at my command,

194
00:07:28,083 --> 00:07:32,250
but current events
somewhat elude me.

195
00:07:33,416 --> 00:07:34,416
Faster.

196
00:07:34,416 --> 00:07:37,208
There's too much hot air
in here.

197
00:07:37,208 --> 00:07:38,833
The Merged Lands
are being attacked.

198
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:41,541
Spectral beings
are hollowing people out.

199
00:07:41,541 --> 00:07:44,333
They got Roby
and countless others so far.

200
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:47,250
I've read of such
Spectral Invasions,

201
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:50,041
but never imagined
it could actually happen.

202
00:07:50,041 --> 00:07:52,458
There's this dragon,
ThunderFang.

203
00:07:52,458 --> 00:07:54,791
We stopped him once,
and he died,

204
00:07:54,791 --> 00:07:56,375
but that didn't slow him down

205
00:07:56,375 --> 00:07:58,000
as much as you'd expect.

206
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,333
There are some things
that only grow stronger

207
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:03,041
in the rot of death.

208
00:08:03,041 --> 00:08:04,375
I'm not surprised

209
00:08:04,375 --> 00:08:06,916
that blasphemous old lizard
is one of them.

210
00:08:06,916 --> 00:08:09,333
He tried to become
a Source Dragon.

211
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:12,083
Such unthinkable heresy
is beyond evil.

212
00:08:12,083 --> 00:08:15,125
He was once defeated here
in the City of Temples, right?

213
00:08:15,125 --> 00:08:17,083
We need you to teach us
how it was done.

214
00:08:17,083 --> 00:08:19,541
I can not only tell you,

215
00:08:19,541 --> 00:08:21,458
I can show you,

216
00:08:21,458 --> 00:08:23,916
but not from this cell.

217
00:08:23,916 --> 00:08:25,916
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
what are you trying to pull?

218
00:08:25,916 --> 00:08:27,208
Professor Pompous here

219
00:08:27,208 --> 00:08:29,708
knows all the secret passages
in this place.

220
00:08:29,708 --> 00:08:31,000
As soon as our backs
are turned,

221
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,041
he's gonna bolt

222
00:08:32,041 --> 00:08:33,833
and turn on the booby traps
or something.

223
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:35,041
Bleckt might be a villain,

224
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:37,375
but he loves the Source Dragons.

225
00:08:37,375 --> 00:08:40,000
He understands the stakes here
better than anyone.

226
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,416
Stakes, schmakes!

227
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:42,416
We can't free this clown

228
00:08:42,416 --> 00:08:44,458
after he tried
to get rid of Roby.

229
00:08:44,458 --> 00:08:46,541
Her logic is terrible,

230
00:08:46,541 --> 00:08:48,708
but her conclusion is right.

231
00:08:48,708 --> 00:08:50,125
You can't let him out.

232
00:08:50,125 --> 00:08:51,125
He looks frail,

233
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:53,041
but his knowledge
makes him dangerous!

234
00:08:53,041 --> 00:08:55,333
More dangerous
than what's out there already?

235
00:08:55,333 --> 00:08:56,375
I agree with Sora.

236
00:08:56,375 --> 00:08:57,916
I vote we take the risk.

237
00:08:57,916 --> 00:09:00,458
It's not really
a voting situation.

238
00:09:00,458 --> 00:09:02,000
There's only one person here

239
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,208
with the authority
to free a prisoner.

240
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:05,541
Your call, Wyldfyre.

241
00:09:05,541 --> 00:09:07,416
What's it going to be?

242
00:09:09,875 --> 00:09:11,000
[Cole] I'm taking him down!

243
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,875
[Kai] You can't just run off.

244
00:09:12,875 --> 00:09:15,541
Nokt's one of the most dangerous
of the Forbidden Five.

245
00:09:15,541 --> 00:09:16,916
Remember what he did to me?

246
00:09:16,916 --> 00:09:18,208
I need to get
the Finders' souls

247
00:09:18,208 --> 00:09:19,958
out of that...
thing he's playing!

248
00:09:19,958 --> 00:09:21,166
[Frak] How?

249
00:09:21,166 --> 00:09:23,541
Even our Prismatic Blades
barely hurt these creatures.

250
00:09:23,541 --> 00:09:25,500
That's what
I was trying to say!

251
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,625
When we learned what
was happening in other lands,

252
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:29,791
these weird things attacking,

253
00:09:29,791 --> 00:09:32,583
the Advanced Science Lab
designed new Prismatic Blades

254
00:09:32,583 --> 00:09:34,416
to eliminate them permanently.

255
00:09:34,416 --> 00:09:35,666
Then why aren't we
using them?

256
00:09:35,666 --> 00:09:37,750
They're designed, not built.

257
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:41,041
We need Prismatic Steel
forged with soul energy,

258
00:09:41,041 --> 00:09:43,625
and we only had barely enough
regular Prismatic Ore

259
00:09:43,625 --> 00:09:44,625
for my lenses here.

260
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:46,208
But your blades!

261
00:09:46,208 --> 00:09:49,000
We can upgrade them
and stop these things!

262
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,458
Then what are we waiting for?

263
00:09:50,458 --> 00:09:52,500
We don't have time
to run off to some lab.

264
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,125
Nokt is right there!

265
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:55,666
Cole, stop.

266
00:09:55,666 --> 00:09:57,875
The hot-headed vibe
is usually my thing.

267
00:09:57,875 --> 00:09:58,875
Think this through.

268
00:09:58,875 --> 00:10:00,625
You don't understand.

269
00:10:00,625 --> 00:10:02,500
I should've protected
the Finders.

270
00:10:02,500 --> 00:10:04,583
You're letting your emotions
take over, and--

271
00:10:04,583 --> 00:10:06,208
You're not my teacher, Kai!

272
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:09,541
Protect Percival
and get your blades upgraded.

273
00:10:14,625 --> 00:10:16,500
Let's get this done.

274
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:17,750
Fast.

275
00:10:19,583 --> 00:10:21,791
[tires squealing]

276
00:10:23,208 --> 00:10:25,916
I've decided...

277
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:28,541
that I need a shoulder massage
to help me decide.

278
00:10:30,666 --> 00:10:32,083
Wyldfyre...

279
00:10:32,083 --> 00:10:33,458
Okay, fine!

280
00:10:33,458 --> 00:10:35,250
As acting President,
Prime Minister,

281
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:36,708
Boss of the City of Temples,

282
00:10:36,708 --> 00:10:38,458
I've come to a decision.

283
00:10:38,458 --> 00:10:40,041
Release Bleckt.

284
00:10:45,541 --> 00:10:47,583
Don't even think about running.

285
00:10:47,583 --> 00:10:49,166
I never run.

286
00:10:49,166 --> 00:10:51,791
I walk in a stately manner.

287
00:10:51,791 --> 00:10:53,208
Follow me.

288
00:10:53,208 --> 00:10:55,041
The secrets you need

289
00:10:55,041 --> 00:10:57,333
are kept hidden
in the Vault of Focus.

290
00:10:57,333 --> 00:10:58,500
To enter the vault,

291
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:01,000
I must speak the pass-phrase.

292
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,708
Turn around
and cover your ears.

293
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:06,541
Yeah, right. We turn, you run.

294
00:11:06,541 --> 00:11:08,250
We're not
taking our eyes off you.

295
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,041
Make with the pass-phrase,
Bleckty.

296
00:11:10,041 --> 00:11:11,791
[grumbling]

297
00:11:12,791 --> 00:11:14,541
I hereby acknowledge

298
00:11:14,541 --> 00:11:16,958
that Roby is so dope

299
00:11:16,958 --> 00:11:18,916
that I can't even.

300
00:11:18,916 --> 00:11:20,958
Zoot-zoot.

301
00:11:21,791 --> 00:11:23,416
[laughing]

302
00:11:23,416 --> 00:11:25,833
[mechanism clanking]

303
00:11:25,833 --> 00:11:27,791
Hmm, probably a trap.

304
00:11:27,791 --> 00:11:30,125
Next one down that pole
is a goner.

305
00:11:30,125 --> 00:11:32,666
Your funeral, Greenie.

306
00:11:35,791 --> 00:11:37,375
Oh, well,
it was nice knowing him.

307
00:11:37,375 --> 00:11:38,458
I mean, not really.
[chuckling]

308
00:11:38,458 --> 00:11:39,541
So neurotic.

309
00:11:39,541 --> 00:11:41,291
[Lloyd calling] Ninja!

310
00:11:41,291 --> 00:11:43,125
It's okay, I'm safe!

311
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:45,250
But, well...

312
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:46,125
it's a lot.

313
00:11:46,125 --> 00:11:47,750
Come see.

314
00:11:52,958 --> 00:11:55,083
Is this all built with...

315
00:11:55,083 --> 00:11:56,666
[Bleckt] Prismatic Steel.

316
00:11:56,666 --> 00:12:00,000
The City of Temples
sits on a deposit of raw ore.

317
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,875
It was mixed with soul energy

318
00:12:01,875 --> 00:12:04,833
to create the chains
for ThunderFang,

319
00:12:04,833 --> 00:12:07,791
the Shatter Dragon of Chaos.

320
00:12:07,791 --> 00:12:11,125
Chaos is
an almost unstoppable force,

321
00:12:11,125 --> 00:12:14,708
but it has a natural enemy...

322
00:12:14,708 --> 00:12:16,000
Focus.

323
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,125
[tapping pillar]

324
00:12:18,833 --> 00:12:21,250
That's
the Source Dragon of Focus?

325
00:12:21,250 --> 00:12:22,500
No.

326
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,875
The Arc Dragon of Focus,

327
00:12:24,875 --> 00:12:28,291
a mortal avatar
of the Focus Source Dragon.

328
00:12:28,291 --> 00:12:31,375
Only the Council of Sources
can vote to release it.

329
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:34,541
We can't count on the vote
going our way this time.

330
00:12:34,541 --> 00:12:35,791
I have reason to believe

331
00:12:35,791 --> 00:12:37,541
the Source Dragons
are deadlocked

332
00:12:37,541 --> 00:12:38,958
about helping mortals.

333
00:12:38,958 --> 00:12:42,875
If that's true,
then chaos will reign.

334
00:12:42,875 --> 00:12:44,458
But I've heard
there's a way for mortals

335
00:12:44,458 --> 00:12:46,416
to wake the Arc Dragon of Focus.

336
00:12:47,416 --> 00:12:49,166
There might be,

337
00:12:49,166 --> 00:12:52,083
but the consequences
could be disastrous.

338
00:12:52,083 --> 00:12:55,375
We never back down
from disastrous consequences.

339
00:12:55,375 --> 00:12:57,375
Even when we really should.

340
00:12:57,375 --> 00:12:59,958
Summoning
the Source Dragons' champion

341
00:12:59,958 --> 00:13:01,416
without their permission

342
00:13:01,416 --> 00:13:04,208
could mark you as an enemy
of the Sources.

343
00:13:04,208 --> 00:13:05,333
But if we don't,

344
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:06,916
ThunderFang could destroy
the Source Dragons

345
00:13:06,916 --> 00:13:08,500
and the Merged Lands.

346
00:13:09,625 --> 00:13:12,458
If you're going to risk
such an action,

347
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:14,833
you will need this...

348
00:13:16,208 --> 00:13:18,958
...the Unbidden Storm.

349
00:13:21,708 --> 00:13:25,291
[spectral note reverberating]

350
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:31,958
[heroic music playing]

351
00:13:39,791 --> 00:13:40,791
[screaming]

352
00:13:52,833 --> 00:13:55,125
Hurry, Cole's out there alone!

353
00:13:58,291 --> 00:14:00,041
[power surging]

354
00:14:00,041 --> 00:14:02,875
It has never been done,

355
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:05,583
but when the Arc Dragon of Focus
is inactive,

356
00:14:05,583 --> 00:14:07,750
it rests
the two halves of itself

357
00:14:07,750 --> 00:14:09,208
in two caves.

358
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:11,625
Each must be awakened separately

359
00:14:11,625 --> 00:14:13,541
by a spell-song,

360
00:14:13,541 --> 00:14:15,291
this song--

361
00:14:15,291 --> 00:14:18,750
[bells chiming]

362
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:21,250
--exactly note by note.

363
00:14:21,250 --> 00:14:24,000
[bell song chiming]

364
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,166
Then, once they're awake,

365
00:14:26,166 --> 00:14:28,458
the Unbidden Storm
must be brought to the place

366
00:14:28,458 --> 00:14:30,583
where the Arc Dragon
is to be summoned...

367
00:14:30,583 --> 00:14:31,958
in this case,

368
00:14:31,958 --> 00:14:35,708
as close to ThunderFang's
source of power as possible...

369
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:39,416
but such actions
have never been attempted

370
00:14:39,416 --> 00:14:40,958
by mortals before.

371
00:14:40,958 --> 00:14:43,250
It's the only shot we have.

372
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:44,833
Where are the two halves
of the dragon?

373
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:48,916
One half is in
Mysterium's Cave of Bells,

374
00:14:48,916 --> 00:14:50,500
but the other half,

375
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:52,291
I'm sorry to tell you,

376
00:14:52,291 --> 00:14:54,208
was in Djinjago,

377
00:14:54,208 --> 00:14:55,958
which has been destroyed.

378
00:14:55,958 --> 00:14:58,333
Not anymore. It's back.

379
00:14:58,333 --> 00:15:01,166
ThunderFang and Djinjago
are back?

380
00:15:01,166 --> 00:15:03,125
No one tells me anything!

381
00:15:03,125 --> 00:15:06,291
But Djinjago is only
a sliver of its former self.

382
00:15:06,291 --> 00:15:08,541
So maybe the cave
where this thing sleeps

383
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:09,875
isn't even there yet?

384
00:15:09,875 --> 00:15:12,625
Even if you do wake up
both halves, then what?

385
00:15:12,625 --> 00:15:14,083
March right into
the Spectral Lands

386
00:15:14,083 --> 00:15:15,166
to summon it?

387
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:17,000
You'd be eviscerated
at the border!

388
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,500
[sighing]
Meany-breath has a point.

389
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,541
The last time we entered
the Spectral Lands,

390
00:15:21,541 --> 00:15:23,625
you barely escaped alive.

391
00:15:23,625 --> 00:15:25,083
I mean, I was fine,

392
00:15:25,083 --> 00:15:27,500
but you all? [scoffing]

393
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:30,083
I might have an idea
about that.

394
00:15:30,083 --> 00:15:32,125
Anyone want to visit
the junkyard?

395
00:15:38,583 --> 00:15:40,625
Time for a field test!

396
00:15:50,583 --> 00:15:51,500
H'yah!

397
00:15:54,375 --> 00:15:57,041
This is for the Finders!

398
00:15:59,250 --> 00:16:01,083
[unearthly shrieking]

399
00:16:01,083 --> 00:16:02,541
There they are!

400
00:16:03,625 --> 00:16:05,125
[gasping and struggling]

401
00:16:05,125 --> 00:16:06,291
Cole!

402
00:16:06,291 --> 00:16:07,583
[groaning]

403
00:16:08,625 --> 00:16:11,083
[blowing spectral note]

404
00:16:15,833 --> 00:16:16,833
[revving engine]

405
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,833
H'yah!

406
00:16:18,833 --> 00:16:19,833
[grunting with impact]

407
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:20,916
[panting]

408
00:16:22,541 --> 00:16:23,541
Is he...?

409
00:16:23,541 --> 00:16:24,458
Alive,

410
00:16:24,458 --> 00:16:25,583
but...

411
00:16:25,583 --> 00:16:26,958
he's hollow.

412
00:16:26,958 --> 00:16:29,000
[sighing] Cole,
why didn't you listen?

413
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[unearthly shrieking overhead]

414
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,208
[shrieking]

415
00:16:32,750 --> 00:16:33,958
H'ah!

416
00:16:33,958 --> 00:16:35,333
It works!

417
00:16:35,333 --> 00:16:37,250
[shrieking]

418
00:16:48,208 --> 00:16:49,416
[blowing spectral note]

419
00:16:56,958 --> 00:16:58,041
Nokt!

420
00:16:58,041 --> 00:16:59,791
Your music's terrible!

421
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:21,416
Citizens of Imperium!

422
00:17:21,416 --> 00:17:24,916
Thanks to the Ninja,
once again, our city is free!

423
00:17:24,916 --> 00:17:28,125
[cheering]

424
00:17:29,541 --> 00:17:32,750
[hollowed people moaning]

425
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:35,291
You did it!

426
00:17:35,291 --> 00:17:36,416
But look at the cost.

427
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:44,083
Whatever this Sora kid's up to

428
00:17:44,083 --> 00:17:45,166
better be worth it.

429
00:17:46,791 --> 00:17:48,291
[Lloyd] What are you
looking at, Bleckt?

430
00:17:48,291 --> 00:17:50,708
If ThunderFang
has gathered enough souls

431
00:17:50,708 --> 00:17:52,916
to attempt to become
a Source Dragon,

432
00:17:52,916 --> 00:17:54,833
the immense power
will be visible

433
00:17:54,833 --> 00:17:56,583
from all the Merged Lands.

434
00:17:56,583 --> 00:17:59,208
So it's good
we don't see anything.

435
00:17:59,208 --> 00:18:00,208
[Bleckt] Yet.

436
00:18:11,875 --> 00:18:13,625
What do you think?

437
00:18:13,625 --> 00:18:16,666
Specially designed
for the Spectral Lands.

438
00:18:16,666 --> 00:18:18,625
I went to the junkyard
to build these mechs,

439
00:18:18,625 --> 00:18:20,000
and Wyldfyre ordered bots

440
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,291
to bring me some Prismatic Ore
to cover them with.

441
00:18:22,291 --> 00:18:25,541
So they're impervious
to spectral attack?

442
00:18:25,541 --> 00:18:27,583
That's not entirely stupid.

443
00:18:27,583 --> 00:18:29,416
More like brilliant!

444
00:18:29,416 --> 00:18:30,708
This is the chance we need

445
00:18:30,708 --> 00:18:33,041
to get all the way
to ThunderFang at the Well!

446
00:18:33,041 --> 00:18:34,458
[Lloyd] Great work, Sora.

447
00:18:34,458 --> 00:18:36,500
Okay, team, we've got a plan,

448
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,416
sort of,

449
00:18:37,416 --> 00:18:38,750
but we have to move fast.

450
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:39,791
Let's go.

451
00:18:39,791 --> 00:18:42,333
The bots will take you
back to your cell,

452
00:18:42,333 --> 00:18:44,958
and if you lied
about any of this,

453
00:18:44,958 --> 00:18:47,000
I'll come back
and authorize your life

454
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,000
to be miserable forever.

455
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,708
I am not betting
on your chances of success.

456
00:18:52,708 --> 00:18:55,000
Always such a downer, Bleckt.

457
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,875
May the Source Dragons
forgive us.

458
00:19:00,416 --> 00:19:03,041
[blowing spectral note]

459
00:19:03,041 --> 00:19:05,625
<i>[ThunderFang] So few souls?</i>

460
00:19:05,625 --> 00:19:09,875
<i>Is not Imperium</i>
<i>a vastly populated land?</i>

461
00:19:12,875 --> 00:19:14,500
[blowing spectral note]

462
00:19:17,708 --> 00:19:21,083
<i>Now, that's more like it.</i>

463
00:19:33,375 --> 00:19:35,250
<i>Finally!</i>

464
00:19:35,250 --> 00:19:40,291
<i>I have collected</i>
<i>all the power I will need!</i>

465
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,541
[distant thunder rumbling]

466
00:19:46,541 --> 00:19:48,375
[Lloyd] Bleckt warned us
this was coming.

467
00:19:48,375 --> 00:19:50,583
We've gotta go now!

468
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,708
Okay, last time. Arin?

469
00:19:55,708 --> 00:19:57,916
You and I will take
this Unbidden Storm thing

470
00:19:57,916 --> 00:19:59,291
to the Well of the Lost,

471
00:19:59,291 --> 00:20:02,083
and can summon the Arc Dragon
once its two halves are awake.

472
00:20:02,083 --> 00:20:03,875
Good. Sora and Wyldfyre?

473
00:20:03,875 --> 00:20:06,291
We'll get Zanth
to take us to Djinjago.

474
00:20:06,291 --> 00:20:08,375
If this Cave of Tones exists,

475
00:20:08,375 --> 00:20:10,166
which I really hope it does,

476
00:20:10,166 --> 00:20:11,750
we ring the Spell Song.

477
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,666
Okay. Nya and Jay?

478
00:20:13,666 --> 00:20:14,666
[Nya] We'll go to Mysterium,

479
00:20:14,666 --> 00:20:15,791
ring the spell song,

480
00:20:15,791 --> 00:20:17,291
and wake the dragon's
other half.

481
00:20:17,291 --> 00:20:19,750
Yeah, except I'm not doing
any of that.

482
00:20:20,333 --> 00:20:22,083
I've already done
more than I bargained for

483
00:20:22,083 --> 00:20:23,333
on this little trip.

484
00:20:23,333 --> 00:20:25,541
You can't bail
on saving the world.

485
00:20:25,541 --> 00:20:27,083
That's not what Ninja do.

486
00:20:27,083 --> 00:20:29,166
I'm not a ninja!

487
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:31,500
Why can't you all get that
through your heads?

488
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:33,541
You hired me for one job!

489
00:20:33,541 --> 00:20:35,833
I did it,
and you still haven't paid me

490
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:38,125
or helped me capture Ras!

491
00:20:38,125 --> 00:20:40,500
I thought Ninja
kept their word.

492
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:42,291
We've been a little busy.

493
00:20:42,291 --> 00:20:45,000
Yeah. Busy
nearly getting me killed,

494
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,208
and I'm done.

495
00:20:46,208 --> 00:20:47,541
I really believed,

496
00:20:47,541 --> 00:20:49,291
after all we'd been through,

497
00:20:49,291 --> 00:20:51,625
that you'd care about
something other than yourself.

498
00:20:51,625 --> 00:20:53,833
I thought I saw glimpses
of your old self,

499
00:20:53,833 --> 00:20:56,166
moments
where you knew the truth,

500
00:20:56,166 --> 00:20:58,458
that you were a hero,

501
00:20:58,458 --> 00:21:00,500
but I was wrong.

502
00:21:02,041 --> 00:21:06,125
Try not to die
before you pay me.

503
00:21:08,833 --> 00:21:11,291
Nya, if you--

504
00:21:11,291 --> 00:21:14,083
Lloyd,
we've got a world to save.

505
00:21:15,916 --> 00:21:16,875
[Wyldfyre gasping]

506
00:21:20,750 --> 00:21:22,333
Good luck, everybody!

507
00:21:26,583 --> 00:21:28,625
We're gonna need it.

508
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:34,416
[gates closing]

509
00:21:41,625 --> 00:21:42,666
[Ras growling]

510
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

